# Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy describes how Example University's PanelMaker instance collects, uses, and shares information when you visit or use the site.

## Who Is Responsible

Example University, Institute of Spatial Biology
Example Street 1, 12345 Example City, Germany
[panelmaker@example.edu](mailto:panelmaker@example.edu)

## Information We Collect

We collect standard server log data (IP address, browser type, referring/exit pages, timestamps) and only the cookies strictly necessary for the operation of the site: the Auth.js session cookies that keep you signed in and a cookie that remembers the sidebar state. No analytics or tracking cookies are used.

If you create an account, we also collect the information you provide directly, such as your name, email address, and any content you submit.

## Hosting

This instance is hosted on infrastructure operated by Example University's IT department.

## Your Rights

If you are in the European Economic Area, you have the right to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of your personal data, and to object to or restrict its processing. Contact us using the details above to exercise these rights.

## Contact

For privacy questions, contact [panelmaker@example.edu](mailto:panelmaker@example.edu).
